# Version pins for the toolchain (feat-5-foundation-monorepo-ci, REQ-003).
#
# This is the one source of truth for the versions of the tools. The install
# scripts (.specmgr/feat/feat-5-foundation-monorepo-ci/bin/) read it. The CI
# workflow repeats the versions as inputs of the setup actions, and a `just`
# recipe checks that both are the same (ACC-013).
#
# Format: KEY=value, no spaces, no quotes. A shell can source this file.
#
# Checksums: the values are copied from the files that the vendors publish
# (Temurin: the API of Adoptium; Maven: the .sha512 file; Node: SHASUMS256.txt;
# pnpm: the digest of the GitHub release; just: SHA256SUMS; npm and Maven Central:
# the checksum of the release). The Python tools have no checksum in this file: their
# lock files in tools/python/ have them. A change of a version must change the
# checksum, or the lock file, in the same commit. CODEOWNERS covers this file.
#
# What is checked with a checksum, and what is not (finding G2 of the review):
#
#   Install scripts (machine of the author): the JDK, Maven, Node, pnpm and just
#   are compared with the checksum of the download (JDK_SHA256, MAVEN_SHA512,
#   NODE_SHA256, PNPM_SHA256, JUST_SHA256).
#
#   The tools that the gates start in CI and on the machine of the author are
#   checked at run time:
#     - The Python tools (specmgr, PyYAML, license-expression with boolean.py;
#       feat-22-python-tools-lockfile): CHECKED, with all their dependencies. The lock
#       files in tools/python/ have the exact version and the sha256 of each file of each
#       package (44 packages for specmgr, 1 for PyYAML, 2 for license-expression). The gate
#       scripts install them with `uv pip install --require-hashes --only-binary :all:` in
#       a virtual environment of PYTHON_VERSION, so uv stops for a wrong hash, for a package
#       with no hash and for a package that is not in the file. No source archive is built.
#       This file has the version of each tool only (SPECMGR_VERSION, PYYAML_VERSION,
#       LICENSE_EXPRESSION_VERSION) and no checksum of them. `just check-pins` compares the
#       lock files with these versions (the procedure to change a version is in
#       tools/python/README.md).
#     - @cyclonedx/cdxgen (feat-16-cdxgen-lockfile): CHECKED, with all its
#       dependencies. tools/sbom/ is a pnpm project with one dependency and a
#       lock file that has an integrity value for each package (199 packages for
#       12.9.0, and 187 are installed on linux-x64). sbom.sh installs it with `pnpm install
#       --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts`, and pnpm compares each tarball with
#       the lock file. `just check-pins` compares package.json and the lock file
#       with CDXGEN_VERSION and CDXGEN_INTEGRITY of this file, so a change of only
#       one of the three places stops the check (the procedure to change the
#       version is in tools/sbom/README.md). Limit: a wrong integrity value of an
#       OPTIONAL dependency does not stop the install. pnpm does not install that
#       package, and the package does not run.
#     - cyclonedx-maven-plugin: sbom.sh compares the sha256 of the jar in the local
#       repository with CYCLONEDX_MAVEN_PLUGIN_SHA256 before the plugin makes the
#       SBOM. The dependencies of the plugin are not checked (GitHub issue #23).
#     - uv itself, the Python build that uv downloads and the GitHub Actions: UV_VERSION
#       has no checksum (the action astral-sh/setup-uv downloads it), and the actions
#       are pinned to a commit SHA.
#
# JDK: Eclipse Temurin 21 (LTS), GPL-2.0-only WITH Classpath-exception-2.0
JDK_VERSION=21.0.13+9
JDK_SHA256=d7f5d5cf865a2902b70ff549b97586a7d3f234e016f041ab447ea740c7d66d1c

# Maven (the 3.x line; Maven 4 is a release candidate), Apache-2.0
MAVEN_VERSION=3.10.0
MAVEN_SHA512=908b1501bfb420bf7c8affb855534a9c407fd6099367bfb9f2f2dcb8e9799102bffb84518cde74c679bd76870247c6528683abdd620581bffa90f95d92d175aa

# Node 26 (LTS "Lithium"), MIT. This release has no corepack.
NODE_VERSION=26.13.0
NODE_SHA256=d28a96af6c38596f6d9d97c0ee531c13d238d757742387d1928de822d959e997

# pnpm (standalone release, no corepack), MIT
PNPM_VERSION=12.16.1
PNPM_SHA256=565ff81174a14f6f7bd5d84c1b17e51031a80230d370a1fe24be5d16bd02a825

# just, CC0-1.0
JUST_VERSION=1.59.0
JUST_SHA256=409044617b6f06517c1035e55ca38c8c856ff8b650e41bc2aa1ef82d5903a23e

# uv, MIT OR Apache-2.0. CI only (the action astral-sh/setup-uv). The machine
# of the author has its own uv, and no install script changes it.
UV_VERSION=0.13.7

# Python for the gates (feat-22-python-tools-lockfile), PSF-2.0 (the class Permitted since 2026-11-04).
# The minor version. The lock files in tools/python/ are valid for each 3.13 release. The gate scripts
# start `uv venv --python 3.13`, and uv downloads a managed Python if no 3.13 is on the machine.
PYTHON_VERSION=3.13

# SBOM tools (feat-5, Task 130.130)
# cyclonedx-maven-plugin, Apache-2.0 (the checksum is for the jar)
CYCLONEDX_MAVEN_PLUGIN_VERSION=2.9.3
CYCLONEDX_MAVEN_PLUGIN_SHA256=c452d5eebe28bc86bef2e7c72d129f04f60877bef843eac8120f01fb655be293
# @cyclonedx/cdxgen, Apache-2.0 (the integrity value of the npm package). The lock file
# tools/sbom/pnpm-lock.yaml and tools/sbom/package.json must have the same values
# (just check-pins checks it). Change all three places in one commit: tools/sbom/README.md.
CDXGEN_VERSION=12.9.0
CDXGEN_INTEGRITY=sha512-+LWBiyTgdSWdprdsA7xpNEhD9NV/Wo3TvqaVYQHjP3kEeNEZTV+08U8CYh+P2+2CHycwKFWHhtSREN+p/r6Sgw==

# Python tools of the gates (feat-5, Tasks 130.110 to 130.142; feat-22-python-tools-lockfile). These are
# the direct tools. Their dependencies and all checksums are in the lock files in tools/python/
# (just check-pins compares the version of each tool in its lock file with the version here).
# These tools do not go to users, so rule A applies (only the main license).
# license-expression, Apache-2.0 (the wheel has a data file under CC-BY-4.0). Its dependency
# boolean.py (BSD-2-Clause) is in tools/python/license-expression.lock.
LICENSE_EXPRESSION_VERSION=30.4.4
# specmgr (the PyPI package biz-dfch-specmgr), AGPL-3.0-or-later
SPECMGR_VERSION=0.38.0
# PyYAML, MIT (the gates for workflows read the YAML with it)
PYYAML_VERSION=6.0.3
